          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "warning",
          "guid": "mt28aggys5igkgzl",
          "message": {
            "text": "positionBelowAnchor now returns a disposer that MUST be called on dismissal — a bare el.remove() leaks the autoReposition scroll/resize listeners. Switching from the one-shot positionAnchored to autoReposition (so popups follow a moving anchor) means the placement now owns capture-phase scroll + resize listeners. They are only removed by the returned disposer, so every caller has to route all its close paths through it. Both current callers do (riskPopover.tsx, reclassifyPopup.tsx funnel reopen / option-pick / outside-click through a single tracked dismiss). The project's heap-stability e2e (stability.test.ts) would catch a regression here.\n",
            "markdown": "`positionBelowAnchor` now returns a disposer that MUST be called on dismissal — a bare `el.remove()` leaks the autoReposition scroll/resize listeners. Switching from the one-shot `positionAnchored` to `autoReposition` (so popups follow a moving anchor) means the placement now owns capture-phase `scroll` + `resize` listeners. They are only removed by the returned disposer, so every caller has to route **all** its close paths through it. Both current callers do (`riskPopover.tsx`, `reclassifyPopup.tsx` funnel reopen / option-pick / outside-click through a single tracked `dismiss`). The project's heap-stability e2e (`stability.test.ts`) would catch a regression here.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/popup.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 34,
                  "endLine": 34,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  return autoReposition(el, anchor, { gap: gapPx });"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
